(vector (map (:adr/consequences "{:positive [\"Publishing of directories and mailing lists (5812) now genuinely\\n    implemented and fully tested as a coordination-only actor, following\\n    this fleet's established pattern\" \"The coordination-not-data-privacy-compliance-authority boundary is a\\n    hard, permanent, unconditional governor block (any proposal directly\\n    finalizing a GDPR/CCPA compliance decision, a deletion/erasure\\n    resolution, or a right-to-be-forgotten grant) plus a structural\\n    phase-table absence for :flag-privacy-concern -- two independent layers\\n    agree, not just asserted in prose, satisfying ADR-2607152500's Wave-4\\n    person-facing-service safety guardrail\" \"Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs\"], :negative [\"Still a simulation/proposal layer -- single MemStore backend, mock\\n    advisor, no real directory-management-system integration. Same\\n    limitation as every sibling actor in this fleet at this stage\" \"The privacy-compliance-decision scope-exclusion term list is a STARTING\\n    catalog (English/Japanese GDPR/CCPA/right-to-be-forgotten/DSAR\\n    terminology), not an exhaustive survey of every jurisdiction's\\n    data-protection-law vocabulary -- documented plainly as a scope\\n    limitation, not silently generalized\"]}"), (:adr/scope-exclusions (vector "directly finalizing a data-privacy-compliance decision (deciding a\n   listing/subscriber record is GDPR/CCPA/opt-out compliant) -- permanently\n   blocked, no override" "resolving or granting a data-subject deletion/erasure/'right to be\n   forgotten' request -- permanently blocked, no override" "any other privacy-authority determination (consent adjudication,\n   regulatory compliance ruling) -- permanently blocked, no override" "coverage beyond the seeded English/Japanese GDPR/CCPA/right-to-be-\n   forgotten/DSAR terminology in the scope-exclusion term list -- a starting\n   catalog, not an exhaustive survey of every jurisdiction's data-protection\n   vocabulary")), (:adr/related (vector "ADR-2607121000 (wave rollout plan)" "ADR-2607152500 (Wave 4 human-facing/personal-services authorization + person-facing-service safety guardrail)" "ADR fresh-scaffold protocol per cloud-itonami-isic-873 (residential care, closest architectural sibling)")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "adr-2616000000-cloud-itonami-isic-5812-directories-mailing-lists-coverage"), (:adr/context "Live kotoba-lang/industry registry re-verified fresh before work began: :name\n  'Publishing of directories and mailing lists' confirmed for {:id \"5812\"}\n  (:maturity :spec, stale placeholder :repo/:business-id\n  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5812 predating the current cloud-itonami-isic-<id>\n  naming convention). No prior cloud-itonami-isic-5812 repo existed (gh api\n  404, confirmed before this work began). Built from cloud-itonami-isic-873\n  (residential care activities for the elderly and disabled) as the\n  module-structure template -- closest architectural sibling: same\n  coordination-only shape, same closed op-allowlist pattern, same\n  record-verification/effect-propose/scope-exclusion gate structure. ISIC\n  5812 covers publishing of directories (telephone/business/trade\n  directories, compilations of facts) and mailing lists (subscriber/address\n  lists). This activity directly touches personal-data handling and\n  privacy/consent decisions -- directory entries and mailing-list records\n  routinely contain PII, and publishers are frequently the subject of\n  opt-out/deletion/accuracy-dispute requests. Per the Wave-4 person-facing-\n  service safety guardrail (ADR-2607152500), the closed op allowlist NEVER\n  includes an op that directly finalizes a data-privacy-compliance decision\n  -- those are always either a hard permanent block or an always-escalate\n  op, never auto-commit-eligible; any 'flag a concern' op always escalates\n  and is never in any phase's :auto set."), (:adr/adr-id "2616000000"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2616000000: cloud-itonami ISIC 5812 (Publishing of directories and mailing lists) actor coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted. `cloud-itonami-isic-5812` scaffolded fresh (no prior repo\nexisted — confirmed via `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5812`\n404 before this work began) and landed at\n`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5812`, following\nthe verified fresh-scaffold protocol established across this fleet\n(closest architectural sibling: `cloud-itonami-isic-873`, residential\ncare activities for the elderly and disabled — same coordination-only,\nindependent-Governor, Phase 0→3 rollout shape). Part of the fleet's\nWave 4 batch (human-facing/personal services, ISIC sections I/P/Q/R/S/T,\nADR-2607152500), which was authorized to proceed in parallel with the\njust-completed Wave 3 (production/robotics, ADR-2607121000).\n\n## Context\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry`'s `resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn`\ncarried `{:id \"5812\", :name \"Publishing of directories and mailing\nlists\", ...}` at `:maturity :spec` with a stale placeholder\n`:repo`/`:business-id` (`https://github.com/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5812`\n/ `cloud-itonami-J5812`) predating the current `cloud-itonami-isic-<id>`\nnaming convention. The live `:name` was independently re-verified\nagainst a fresh clone before any work began, per this fleet's ID/name-\nmismatch caution, and confirmed to match \"Publishing of directories and\nmailing lists\" exactly. This work implements the blueprint as a real,\ntested `cloud-itonami-isic-<id>` actor repo and corrects the registry\nentry's `:repo`/`:business-id` fields to match.\n\nISIC 5812 covers publishing of directories (telephone directories,\nbusiness/trade directories, other compilations of facts) and mailing\nlists (subscriber lists, address lists sold or licensed for direct-mail\nor other commercial use). This activity touches personal-data handling\nand privacy/consent decisions directly — directory entries and mailing-\nlist records routinely contain personally identifiable information\n(names, addresses, phone numbers), and publishers are frequently the\nsubject of data-subject opt-out, deletion, and accuracy-dispute\nrequests. Per this fleet's Wave-4 person-facing-service safety\nguardrail (ADR-2607152500), the closed op allowlist for this actor\nNEVER includes any op that directly finalizes a data-privacy-compliance\ndecision (deciding a listing is GDPR/CCPA/opt-out compliant, resolving\na data-subject deletion/erasure request, granting a \"right to be\nforgotten\" claim) — those are always either a hard, permanent block or\nan always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible.\n\n## Decision\n\nScaffold `cloud-itonami-isic-5812` mirroring the `cloud-itonami-isic-873`\n(residential care) architecture closely — same langgraph-clj StateGraph\n+ independent Governor + Phase 0→3 rollout pattern, same\nrecord-verification/effect-propose/scope-exclusion gate structure — but\nretargeted to directory/mailing-list publishing's own domain and\nprivacy-safety profile:\n\n- Namespace prefix `dirmailops` (module `dirmailops`).\n- Governor keyword `:dirmail-governor`.\n- Closed 4-op allowlist, all `:effect :propose` only:\n  `:log-listing-record` (directory-entry/subscriber-list data logging),\n  `:schedule-publication-operation` (compilation/update/print-run\n  scheduling proposal), `:coordinate-distribution` (outbound\n  directory/list distribution coordination), `:flag-privacy-concern`\n  (surface a data-consent/opt-out/accuracy concern — ALWAYS escalates).\n  None of these four ops directly finalizes a data-privacy-compliance\n  decision, satisfying the Wave-4 guardrail by construction.\n- Three HARD governor checks, all permanent and un-overridable by any\n  human approval: (1) the target listing/subscriber record must exist\n  AND be independently `:registered?`/`:verified?` in the store before\n  ANY proposal for it may commit or even escalate — re-derived from the\n  record's own store state, never trusting a proposal's own claim; (2)\n  `:effect` must always be `:propose` — any other value is a claim to\n  directly actuate outside governance; (3) scope exclusion — a fourth\n  check folded into the same rule as the closed-allowlist check — any\n  proposal (regardless of op) whose text touches directly finalizing a\n  data-privacy-compliance decision (GDPR/CCPA compliance determination,\n  a resolved deletion/erasure request, a granted \"right to be\n  forgotten\" claim, a consent-compliance ruling) is a HARD, PERMANENT\n  block, evaluated unconditionally on every proposal.\n- One SOFT escalation gate: LLM confidence below the floor (0.6), OR\n  the op is `:flag-privacy-concern` — ALWAYS escalates to a human,\n  regardless of confidence. `dirmailops.phase` independently agrees:\n  `:flag-privacy-concern` is structurally absent from every phase's\n  `:auto` set, including phase 3 — a permanent fact, not a rollout\n  milestone still to come, matching the Wave-4 guardrail's \"any 'flag a\n  concern' op must always escalate and must never be in any phase's\n  `:auto` set\" requirement.\n- `:log-listing-record`, `:schedule-publication-operation`, and\n  `:coordinate-distribution` MAY auto-commit at phase 3 when the\n  governor is completely clean — matching `cloud-itonami-isic-873`'s\n  own shape (care-note logging / family-visit / supply-request / staff-\n  shift proposals all auto-eligible, only the safety-concern flag\n  permanently excluded).\n- Fully portable `.cljc`, zero JVM-only interop anywhere in `src/`.\n\n## Verification\n\nActor repo built from a uniquely-named scratch dir\n(`/private/tmp/.../scratchpad/5812-work/cloud-itonami-isic-5812`),\nnever touching the shared `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry` checkout:\n\n```\n$ clojure -M:test\nRan 43 tests containing 132 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n\nPushed to `main` at commit `0a925b056bb049ce2d9c9edecc00194c8e058ae4` (`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5812`).\nRe-verified from an INDEPENDENT fresh clone — see the task's final\nreport for the exact re-verification `clojure -M:test` output.\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry` registry: `\"5812\"` entry promoted `:spec` ->\n`:implemented`, `:repo`/`:business-id` corrected from the stale\n`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5812` placeholder to\n`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5812` /\n`cloud-itonami-isic-5812`, exact in-place edit of only the `\"5812\"`\nentry's block (no other entry touched). `test/kotoba/industry_test.clj`\nmaturity-count assertion bumped to the freshly recomputed true\n`:implemented` count (via `kotoba.industry/maturity-summary`, not\n`grep -c`) at edit time — see the task's final report for the exact\nbefore/after counts and merge SHA.\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) ISIC 5812 now has a documented, governed, auditable directory/\nmailing-list-publishing-operations-coordination actor, following this\nfleet's established pattern.\n\n(+) The \"coordination, not data-privacy-compliance authority\" boundary\nis a hard, permanent, unconditional governor block (any proposal\ndirectly finalizing a GDPR/CCPA compliance decision, a deletion/erasure\nresolution, or a \"right to be forgotten\" grant) plus a structural\nphase-table absence for `:flag-privacy-concern` — two independent\nlayers agree, not just asserted in prose, satisfying ADR-2607152500's\nWave-4 person-facing-service safety guardrail.\n\n(+) Portable `.cljc`, zero JVM-only constructs.\n\n(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer — single `MemStore` backend, mock\nadvisor, no real directory-management-system integration. Same\nlimitation as every sibling actor in this fleet at this stage.\n\n(-) The privacy-compliance-decision scope-exclusion term list is a\nSTARTING catalog (GDPR/CCPA/right-to-be-forgotten/DSAR terminology in\nEnglish and Japanese), not an exhaustive survey of every jurisdiction's\ndata-protection-law vocabulary — documented plainly as a scope\nlimitation in `dirmailops.governor`'s own docstring, not silently\ngeneralized."), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)")), (:adr/decision "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-5812 with Advisor/Governor/Phase/Store/\n  Operation/Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-873 module-for-module, adapted\n  from residential-care coordination to directory/mailing-list-publishing\n  coordination -- dirmailops.* namespace, DirMail Governor):\n  - Governor: three HARD checks, all permanent and un-overridable --\n    listing/subscriber record must exist AND be independently\n    :registered?/:verified? in the store before ANY proposal for it may\n    commit or even escalate (re-derived from the record's own store state,\n    never proposal self-report); :effect must always be :propose; scope\n    exclusion (folded together with the closed-op-allowlist check) blocks\n    any proposal, regardless of op, whose text touches directly finalizing\n    a data-privacy-compliance decision. One SOFT escalation gate: low\n    confidence OR the op is :flag-privacy-concern (ALWAYS escalates,\n    regardless of confidence).\n  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate, :flag-privacy-concern permanently absent from\n    every phase's :auto set (structural, not a milestone) -- independently\n    verified by a dedicated test\n    (flag-privacy-concern-never-in-any-auto-set); :log-listing-record,\n    :schedule-publication-operation, and :coordinate-distribution ARE\n    auto-eligible at phase 3.\n  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (default), String-keyed listing\n    directory, append-only ledger + publication-log, 3 seeded demo listings\n    (2 registered+verified, 1 registered-but-unverified to exercise the\n    HARD-hold path).\n  - Advisor: mock-advisor (deterministic, default), same proposal-EDN\n    contract as every sibling actor; a dedicated test\n    (no-proposal-ever-drafts-a-privacy-compliance-decision) asserts no\n    default-path proposal text ever claims to finalize a privacy-compliance\n    decision.\n  - Operation: full langgraph-clj StateGraph (advise -> govern -> decide ->\n    commit|hold|request-approval), real interrupt-before/resume approval\n    workflow.\n  - Sim: demo runner (-main) exercising the full happy path plus HARD-hold\n    scenarios directly.\n  - Ops (closed allowlist, all :effect :propose): log-listing-record\n    (directory-entry/subscriber-list data logging),\n    schedule-publication-operation (compilation/update/print-run scheduling\n    proposal), coordinate-distribution (outbound directory/list\n    distribution coordination), flag-privacy-concern (data-consent/opt-out/\n    accuracy concern -- ALWAYS escalates). None of these four ops directly\n    finalizes a data-privacy-compliance decision, satisfying the Wave-4\n    guardrail by construction.\n  - Tests: 43 tests / 132 assertions across\n    advisor/governor/governor-contract/phase/store-contract, all green.\n  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later.\n  - GitHub repo created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-5812 (no rename\n    fallback needed)."), (:adr/date "2026-07-16"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/verification "{:test-count 43, :assertion-count 132, :test-status \"0 failures, 0 errors (clojure -M:test, both scratch-dir build AND independent fresh re-clone)\", :repo \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5812\", :repo-note \"created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-5812 -- no rename fallback needed\", :commit-sha \"0a925b056bb049ce2d9c9edecc00194c8e058ae4\", :registry-update \"kotoba-lang/industry: 5812 maturity :spec -> :implemented, repo/business-id corrected from stale gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5812 placeholder to cloud-itonami-isic-5812, ADR reference added -- SHAs recorded in the task's final report, not duplicated here\"}"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-5812 (publishing of directories and mailing lists) publishing-operations-coordination actor"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))